<?php

namespace Database\Seeders\Data;

/**
 * The platform product catalogue, as data.
 *
 * This is the whole catalogue and the only copy of it that is version controlled. It replaced
 * storage/app/private/master_materials.csv on 2026-10-08 - a spreadsheet mapped by COLUMN POSITION,
 * read by a 242-line parser, living behind an exception to the blanket storage/ ignore rule. A
 * misplaced comma in that file put a value in the wrong column and imported cleanly; here a row
 * names every field it sets, so it cannot.
 *
 * ## Two columns are missing on purpose
 *
 * nesting_algo and nominal_units are ProductRules::DERIVED - the category decides them, and a row
 * that set them could disagree with its own implementation while looking perfectly ordinary.
 * MasterMaterialsSeeder fills them in. Anything else a row leaves out is null, which is why the
 * rows are ragged: most products have no precise_length and only pipe has a wall.
 *
 * ## Editing it
 *
 * Adding a product is adding a line. REMOVING one is not the inverse: pieces, bars and offcuts
 * carry no product_id - they denormalise the spec and join on it field by field - so deleting a
 * product that work is matched to orphans that work silently, with no foreign key to stop it. That
 * is why a row absent from this file is DEPRECATED rather than deleted wherever anything is using
 * it, and deleted only where nothing is. See Services\ProductUsage.
 *
 * Changing a SPEC column on an existing row is the same hazard wearing a different hat: it does not
 * correct the product, it detaches every piece matched to the old spec and describes a new one.
 * Services\ProductSpec::keyFor() says which columns those are, per category.
 *
 * ## Keeping it honest
 *
 * MasterMaterialsSeederTest plans this whole file through ProductRules against an empty database.
 * It has to come back with zero errors, because that is the question "can the catalogue rebuild
 * itself" and the answer used to be no - the CSV carried 25 rows that no validated path would have
 * accepted, and they were only ever inserted raw.
 */
